Publish a disk0 registry entry with the storage size, for MobileGestalt (Settings showed a capacity of 0 KB).
MobileGestalt's NANDSize() (libMobileGestalt+0xac00) is IOServiceGetMatchingService(IOBSDNameMatching("disk0")) and the
entry's "Size" (kIOMediaSizeKey); it feeds TotalDiskCapacity (Settings > General > About > Capacity, iPhone Storage).
The UFS root is a plain BSD device (ufsroot0), so there was no disk0 ("IOServiceGetMatchingService() for disk0
failed!") and the capacity read 0. The free space is fine (MobileGestalt and FileProvider take it from statfs).
ufs_gpt_find_on_lun() keeps the LUN's size (GPT alternate LBA + 1) when it finds the root partition, and once the
root device exists SweetPlatformExpert.cpp publishes SweetStorageInfo { BSD Name disk0, Size, Whole, Preferred Block
Size }. Not an IOMedia, so nothing matches it as a disk to open or mount.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
